WEBVTT

00:09:29.506 --> 00:09:33.001
I became an incredibly geeky zoning expert,

00:09:33.001 --> 00:09:35.070
finding ways that zoning could address

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:37.132
communities' concerns.

00:09:37.132 --> 00:09:39.704
So little by little, neighborhood by neighborhood,

00:09:39.704 --> 00:09:41.139
block by block,

00:09:41.139 --> 00:09:43.012
we began to set height limits

00:09:43.012 --> 00:09:44.744
so that all new development

00:09:44.744 --> 00:09:48.361
would be predictable and near transit.

00:09:48.361 --> 00:09:50.142
Over the course of 12 years,

00:09:50.142 --> 00:09:52.611
we were able to rezone

00:09:52.611 --> 00:09:55.180
124 neighborhoods,

00:09:55.180 --> 00:09:57.959
40 percent of the city,

00:09:57.959 --> 00:10:02.498
12,500 blocks, so that now,